that"," is"," absent"," from"," the"," platform","'s"," average"," motion","."," The"," minimum"," results"," from"," cancellation"," between"," translation"," and"," rotation",","," rather"," than"," from"," complete"," isolation"," of"," the"," load","."," Moving"," the"," sensor"," changes"," its"," apparent"," location","."," We"," derive"," the"," small","-motion"," equations"," and"," verify"," that"," symmetry"," restores"," dec","ou","pling"," for"," a"," centered"," load","."," Spring"," damping"," is"," represented"," phenomen","ologically",","," and"," large","-angle"," motion"," is"," excluded","."," The"," analysis"," illustrates"," why"," the"," location"," of"," a"," vibration"," measurement"," matters"," when"," comparing"," isol","ators","."," A"," single"," favorable"," trace"," does"," not"," capture"," the"," motion"," of"," the"," whole"," platform","."],"ids_available":true,"boundaries_approximate":false,"piece_format":"native_vocabulary_piece","decoded_text":"Vibration isolation with an off-center suspended load\nA rigid platform is hung from four springs and carries a movable weight. Vertical translation and tilt become coupled when the weight is shifted away from the center. In a calculated frequency sweep, a sensor placed at one corner shows a deep response minimum that is absent from the platform's average motion. The minimum results from cancellation between translation and rotation, rather than from complete isolation of the load. Moving the sensor changes its apparent location. We derive the small-motion equations and verify that symmetry restores decoupling for a centered load. Spring damping is represented phenomenologically, and large-angle motion is excluded. The analysis illustrates why the location of a vibration measurement matters when comparing isolators. A single favorable trace does not capture the motion of the whole platform.","measurement_context":null,"character_measurement":null,"roundtrip_exact":true},{"id":"academic-en-0033","collection":"dataset/academic/en.jsonl","text":"Cache keys for a map tile renderer\nA map renderer is assumed to depend on coordinates, zoom level, style version, and label language. A cache keyed only by coordinates and zoom can return an image that is geometrically correct but linguistically wrong. Adding the language field repairs that collision while leaving style-version collisions unresolved. We enumerate pairs of requests that should share an output and pairs that must remain distinct, using those relations as tests of the key function. The analysis also separates semantic equality from byte equality because compression may vary without changing the rendered content. The principal result is a reproducible method for deriving a cache key from declared dependencies rather than appending fields only after individual stale-output bugs appear.","token_ids":[8232,6894,369,264,2415,10018,19678,198,32,2415,19678,374,19074,311,6761,389,13925,11,15550,2188,11,1707,2319,11,323,2383,4128,13,362,6500,89780,1172,553,13925,323,15550,646,470,458,2168,429,374,52140,745,4396,714,38296,36916,4969,13,30253,279,4128,2070,30069,429,18719,1393,9376,1707,45098,47062,79515,13,1205,13244,13521,315,7388,429,1265,4332,458,2550,323,13521,429,1969,7146,12454,11,1667,1846,4300,438,7032,315,279,1376,729,13,576,6358,1083,61316,41497,21725,504,4922,21725,1576,25034,1231,13281,2041,10013,279,22325,2213,13,576,12429,1102,374,264,52376,77657,1714,369,47787,264,6500,1376,504,14265,19506,4751,1091,92500,5043,1172,1283,3842,50025,59112,22492,4994,13],"tokens":["Cache","Ġkeys","Ġfor","Ġa","Ġmap","Ġtile","Ġrenderer","Ċ","A","Ġmap","Ġrenderer","Ġis","Ġassumed","Ġto","Ġdepend","Ġon","Ġcoordinates",",","Ġzoom","Ġlevel",",","Ġstyle","Ġversion",",","Ġand","Ġlabel","Ġlanguage",".","ĠA","Ġcache","Ġkeyed","Ġonly","Ġby","Ġcoordinates","Ġand","Ġzoom","Ġcan","Ġreturn","Ġan","Ġimage","Ġthat","Ġis","Ġgeometric","ally","Ġcorrect","Ġbut","Ġlingu","istically","Ġwrong",".","ĠAdding","Ġthe","Ġlanguage","Ġfield","Ġrepairs","Ġthat","Ġcollision","Ġwhile","Ġleaving","Ġstyle","-version","Ġcollisions","Ġunresolved",".","ĠWe","Ġenumerate","Ġpairs","Ġof","Ġrequests","Ġthat","Ġshould","Ġshare","Ġan","Ġoutput","Ġand","Ġpairs","Ġthat","Ġmust","Ġremain","Ġdistinct",",","Ġusing","Ġthose","Ġrelations","Ġas","Ġtests","Ġof","Ġthe","Ġkey","Ġfunction",".","ĠThe","Ġanalysis","Ġalso","Ġseparates","Ġsemantic","Ġequality","Ġfrom","Ġbyte","Ġequality","Ġbecause","Ġcompression","Ġmay","Ġvary","Ġwithout","Ġchanging","Ġthe","Ġrendered","Ġcontent",".","ĠThe","Ġprincipal","Ġresult","Ġis","Ġa","Ġrepro","ducible","Ġmethod","Ġfor","Ġderiving","Ġa","Ġcache","Ġkey","Ġfrom","Ġdeclared","Ġdependencies","Ġrather","Ġthan","Ġappending","Ġfields","Ġonly","Ġafter","Ġindividual","Ġstale","-output","Ġbugs","Ġappear","."],"decoded_tokens":["Cache"," keys"," for"," a"," map"," tile"," renderer","\n","A"," map"," renderer"," is"," assumed"," to"," depend"," on"," coordinates",","," zoom"," level",","," style"," version",","," and"," label"," language","."," A"," cache"," keyed"," only"," by"," coordinates"," and"," zoom"," can"," return"," an"," image"," that"," is"," geometric","ally"," correct"," but"," lingu","istically"," wrong","."," Adding"," the"," language"," field"," repairs"," that"," collision"," while"," leaving"," style","-version"," collisions"," unresolved","."," We"," enumerate"," pairs"," of"," requests"," that"," should"," share"," an"," output"," and"," pairs"," that"," must"," remain"," distinct",","," using"," those"," relations"," as"," tests"," of"," the"," key"," function","."," The"," analysis"," also"," separates"," semantic"," equality"," from"," byte"," equality"," because"," compression"," may"," vary"," without"," changing"," the"," rendered"," content","."," The"," principal"," result"," is"," a"," repro","ducible"," method"," for"," deriving"," a"," cache"," key"," from"," declared"," dependencies"," rather"," than"," appending"," fields"," only"," after"," individual"," stale","-output"," bugs"," appear","."],"ids_available":true,"boundaries_approximate":false,"piece_format":"native_vocabulary_piece","decoded_text":"Cache keys for a map tile renderer\nA map renderer is assumed to depend on coordinates, zoom level, style version, and label language. A cache keyed only by coordinates and zoom can return an image that is geometrically correct but linguistically wrong. Adding the language field repairs that collision while leaving style-version collisions unresolved. We enumerate pairs of requests that should share an output and pairs that must remain distinct, using those relations as tests of the key function. The analysis also separates semantic equality from byte equality because compression may vary without changing the rendered content. The principal result is a reproducible method for deriving a cache key from declared dependencies rather than appending fields only after individual stale-output bugs appear.","measurement_context":null,"character_measurement":null,"roundtrip_exact":true},{"id":"academic-ja-0016","collection":"dataset/academic/ja.jsonl","text":"斜光を受ける凹凸面の明暗境界\n細かい溝を持つ模型表面へ、角度を変えて白色光を当てた。撮影の露出を固定すると、照射角が浅いほど溝の境界は明瞭になったが、深い部分の情報は黒くつぶれた。自動露出を使った画像では全体の明るさが補正され、この関係が見えにくくなった。溝の向きと光の向きのなす角を変えると、同じ高さ差でも境界のコントラストが異なる。提案した測度は明るい領域と暗い領域の比率を使うため、反射率が場所ごとに違う面にはそのまま適用できない。模型画像の比較を通じ、画像の見やすさと高さの推定精度が同じ指標ではないことを確認した。模型の寸法や照明設定の範囲を越える普遍的な最適角は示していない。","token_ids":[102372,98683,148793,131545,106412,103906,98389,15755,98478,100316,105813,198,134171,30923,16570,34843,251,136643,58236,100484,101303,130070,5373,100849,29303,130090,130281,102893,98683,29303,98459,36850,27521,1773,123154,98603,15755,107476,29303,101633,134382,5373,112557,99025,28098,101388,16570,134885,34843,251,15755,105813,15310,98478,99940,255,138957,28098,5373,98718,16570,99130,15755,131745,15310,143254,46496,58236,132540,130744,1773,141945,107476,135944,127750,117127,75477,101942,15755,98478,29160,29600,28098,141509,98529,82600,5373,49908,140519,28098,123024,57446,19618,46496,1